course: dictionary
lesson: 13120
title: Flourish: grow, thrive and show off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Flourish» has more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one. Plants need light and water, so when they flourish, they grow well and stay healthy.
explain: «Our little bakery flourished after the new owner arrived.» A bakery cannot grow like a plant, so flourish must mean do very well and be successful. Check by swapping in «did very well». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: «The magician took off his hat with a flourish.» With a flourish means in a showy way, so a flourish can be a big, showy movement. Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence: is it a plant, a business, or a show?
fact: To flourish means to grow well and be healthy, or to do very well and be successful.
fact: Plants flourish with light and water, and children flourish with care.
fact: To flourish something means to wave it around to show it off.
fact: A flourish is a fancy curl in handwriting, or a showy movement or bit of music.
fact: «Flourished» is the past tense, and «flourishing» is the -ing form.
exercise: «The tomato plants flourished in the sunny greenhouse.» What does flourished mean here? | *Grew well and stayed healthy | Turned grey and dried up | Fell over in the wind | Were cut down
exercise: «Our little bakery flourished after the new owner arrived.» What does flourished suggest? | It closed down | It was painted blue | *It did very well and became successful | It got smaller every day
exercise: «The magician took off his hat with a flourish.» What does a flourish mean here? | A sleepy yawn | A puddle | *A showy movement | A small, quiet cough
test: «Children flourish when they feel safe and loved.» Which word is closest in meaning to flourish here? | Shrink | *Thrive | Forget | Argue
test: Which word means to wave something around to show it off? | Whisper | *Flourish | Tuck | Drop
exam: «Her handwriting ended each name with a fancy flourish.» In this sentence, what is a flourish? | *A curly decoration in writing | A kind of cake | A type of shoe | A shower of rain
